  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Owen is trending the right direction. His last two rounds, the Sept 25–26 qualifier at the home course, were 74 (+2) and 71 (−1), and the 71 is his only under-par round in the last ten. He hasn't posted a round since Sept 26, so this is a six-week-old picture.\n\n- **Scoring:** He averaged 76.0 over his last ten rounds and 74.8 over his last five. Those ten average +4.3 to par. The early-July tournament rounds drag that down, including an 82 (+10) at Poplar Grove on July 8. He followed it with 73 and 74 there.\n- **Strokes gained:** These cover 8 of the 10 rounds, because the two qualifier rounds have no stat line. His total is −6.74 per round, against a team average of −4.62, which puts him 6th of 7. There is no college figure for strokes gained. The Tour baseline is 0.\n- **Approach:** This is where he loses the most, at −4.16 per round. The team average is −2.33, and he ranks last of 7.\n- **Putting:** He is the team's strongest putter at −2.06 per round, against a team average of −3.01. The whole team is losing strokes on the greens. He averages 31.88 putts per round over those 8 rounds.\n- **Tee and short game:** Off the tee he is at −0.32, against a team average of +0.87. Around the green he is at −0.20, against a team average of −0.15.\n- **Greens in regulation:** He hit 61.11% over 144 holes. That is above the Division I average of 60%, but below his team average of 66.25% and the Tour figure of 66%.\n\nApproach play is the clearest place to focus. His iron play costs him more than the team average, and his greens-in-regulation rate sits only just above the Division I average.",
